  "warnings": [
    "Two DIFFERENT GitHub-hosted CI runs at different moments; machine identity, CPU contention, software stack and warmup differ. Do not infer head-to-head backend advantage from ratios.",
    "Only the source-level pure counter kernel was identical. Network stacks differ: native C vs Java JDK HTTP. Guest HTTP server sources and full self.forward()/self.backward() semantics are NOT equal.",
    "LLVM private is per-actor OS processes; Graal private is logical PRIVATE ActorRuntime actor and memory isolation, not the same security or cost model.",
    "Fast four-round batches with 1000 requests and 25 warmups/actor do not establish sustainable throughput or unbiased tails. These are NOT 60-second wrk2 tests.",
    "LLVM host native subset recorded no tracing GC; Graal process GC metrics include JVM infrastructure and cannot be attributed solely to actor heaps.",
    "Both implementation branches are draft/unmerged. Full Graal typed guest self.forward()/self.backward() pipeline parity has not been demonstrated by these receipts."
